### Steps to create using Scene Builder

1. Open JavaFX Scene Builder.
2. Create a new FXML document.
3. Drag a VBox from the Containers section into the layout.
4. Drag a Label into the VBox.
5. Set the Label text to `Welcome to JavaFX`.
6. Drag an ImageView into the VBox.
7. Select an image using the ImageView properties.
8. Adjust the ImageView width and height.
9. Set the alignment of VBox to `CENTER`.
10. Save the FXML file.

### Components Used

| Component | Purpose |
| --- | --- |
| VBox | Arranges components vertically |
| Label | Displays text |
| ImageView | Displays an image |

Result: A JavaFX GUI is designed successfully to display text using a Label and an image using an ImageView without writing any Java code.
